meta {
  name: Create Product
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "sku": "WC-TEST-FULL-001",
    "label": "WC Test Full Product",
    "category_ids": ["6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd"],
    "attributes": {"wc_test_text": "WC full-featured test value"},
    "thumbnail_id": "6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.thumbnail_id: eq 6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f
}

docs {
  `POST /api/v3/products` — create a new product. Confirmed live 2026-09-07/08
  against "David's Dev Account". See examples below for: full-featured create (201),
  parent product for a variant flow (201), and missing required field (422).

  ## Key findings

  ### attributes are keyed by attribute NAME, not id
  `{"attributes": {"wc_test_text": "..."}}` — confirmed via a scratch product
  that the key is the attribute's name, not its Mongo `id`. The response's
  `attributes` map also includes account-level system/completeness attributes
  applied automatically to every product (`amazon_ready`,
  `basic_information_completeness`, `website_ready`, etc.).

  ### category_ids links on create — differs from assets
  Unlike `POST /assets` (where `category_ids` is silently ignored on create),
  it works immediately here: a follow-up `GET /products/{id}/categories` shows
  both categories fully linked. Relationship-array fields on create are
  resource-specific — don't assume either way.

  ### thumbnail_id round-trips on create
  This single-reference field persists in the create response. Contrast with
  `category_ids` on assets, which does not.

  ### 201 (not the spec's 200)
  `openapi_pimv3.json` declares `200` only. Live: **201 Created**.

  ### Not idempotent — 409 on duplicate SKU
  Re-running once the fixture exists returns:
  `409 Conflict {"errors":[{"name":"AlreadyExists","description":"product data
  validation failed"}]}` — same `AlreadyExists` family as attribute groups
  (Phase 1), not categories' `422` (quirk #33).

  ### Parent/variant products (Flow 2, confirmed 2026-09-08)
  A variant is created via a second `POST /products` with `parent_id` set to
  the parent's id. After creating the variant:
  - Re-fetching the parent: `product_level` flips from 0 (standalone) to 1
    (parent); `num_variations` increments 0→1.
  - The family's `total_products` count (`GET /product-families/{id}`)
    updates live from 7 to 9.
  - `overwritten_attributes` stays empty when no attribute values are set
    on either product — attribute-inheritance-copying behaviour is not
    exercised unless values are explicitly set.

  ### 422 error envelope
  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"InputDTOValidationError","description":
  "<field>: Field required"}]}` — a flat `errors` array of `{name, description}`
  objects, with `description` naming the missing field directly. Not FastAPI's
  default `HTTPValidationError` shape.
}

example {
  name: 201 - Full Featured Product
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08. Fixture kept as id 6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4. attributes keyed by name (not id). System completeness attributes appear automatically. category_ids links immediately (confirmed via GET /categories follow-up).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "sku": "WC-TEST-FULL-001",
        "label": "WC Test Full Product",
        "category_ids": ["6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd"],
        "attributes": {"wc_test_text": "WC full-featured test value"},
        "thumbnail_id": "6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4",
            "account_id": "6a38f5d5c3d65a5f868b1869",
            "sku": "WC-TEST-FULL-001",
            "label": "WC Test Full Product",
            "gtin": null,
            "status": null,
            "thumbnail_id": "6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f",
            "attributes": {
              "wc_test_text": "WC full-featured test value",
              "amazon_ready": 0.0,
              "basic_information_completeness": 0.0,
              "english_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "google_shopping_completeness": 0.0,
              "marketing_ready": 0.0,
              "product_specifications_completeness": 0.0,
              "shopify_ready": 0.0,
              "spanish_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "website_ready": 0.0
            },
            "parent_id": null,
            "num_variations": 0,
            "product_level": 0,
            "product_type": "SINGLE",
            "product_family_id": null,
            "product_family_model_id": null,
            "overwritten_attributes": [],
            "created": "2026-09-08T14:22:30.000000+00:00",
            "modified": "2026-09-08T14:22:30.000000+00:00",
            "created_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "modified_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            }
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 201 - Parent Product (Variant Flow)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08 (USER_FLOWS.md Flow 2). product_level starts at 0 (standalone) and flips to 1 after a variant is created under it with parent_id set to this product's id. Both parent and variant were deleted in the same test run.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "sku": "WC-TEST-PARENT-001",
        "label": "WC Test Parent",
        "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6aa04a322b6fd055ffb7cae4",
            "account_id": "6a38f5d5c3d65a5f868b1869",
            "sku": "WC-TEST-PARENT-001",
            "label": "WC Test Parent",
            "gtin": null,
            "status": null,
            "thumbnail_id": null,
            "attributes": {
              "amazon_ready": 0.0,
              "basic_information_completeness": 0.0,
              "website_ready": 0.0
            },
            "parent_id": null,
            "num_variations": 0,
            "product_level": 0,
            "product_type": "SINGLE",
            "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e",
            "product_family_model_id": null,
            "overwritten_attributes": [],
            "created": "2026-09-08T15:10:00.000000+00:00",
            "modified": "2026-09-08T15:10:00.000000+00:00",
            "created_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "modified_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            }
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 422 - Missing Required Field (sku)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Omitting sku triggers a 422 with Plytix's custom error envelope — a flat errors array of {name, description} objects, NOT FastAPI's default HTTPValidationError shape.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "label": "Test No SKU"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "sku: Field required"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
